<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila simulans 1.92 µm Turing carrier on the posterior-lobe arc (pass 2) (Drosophila simulans)",
        "Drosophila simulans 1.92 µm Turing carrier on the posterior-lobe arc (pass 2) faithfully reproduces Drosophila simulans morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila simulans specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila simulans" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim GIF-to-plate CV similarity uniquely identifies D. simulans; the whole-fly control also scores 85.6.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of 1.92 µm granule spacing.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the gallery plate is an electron micrograph of the clasper.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: On a 96 µm arc the mode counts are 36 (silvestris), 50 (simulans), 60 (subobscura).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: The plate annulus measures 67.57 µm (111 px scale bar = 100 µm), or 35.2 detail wavelengths per ring.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 1.92 µm is the slot assignment. Neighbour wavelengths 2.64 µm and 1.60 µm are γ retunings.",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards 2007 documents Hawaiian picture-wing melanin; Huey 2000 documents the subobscura size cline.",
        "reported_in_source: Glassford 2015: the epandrial posterior lobe is a melanogaster-subgroup novelty.",
        "reported_in_source: Hagen 2020: simulans-clade lobes diverged within about the last 240,000 years.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a reaction-diffusion instability.",
        "transfer_boundary: Silvestris and subobscura are catalog neighbours at 0 Ma, not phylogenetic ancestors.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 1.92 µm law is not the 83 µm tergite-band model of slot 2701." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila simulans (Cosmopolitan Sister Fruit Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-simulans-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_simulans_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila simulans; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 selects a finite critical wavenumber from a reaction-diffusion instability. | Glassford 2015: the epandrial posterior lobe is a melanogaster-subgroup novelty. | Hagen 2020: simulans-clade lobes diverged within about the last 240,000 years. | Edwards 2007 documents Hawaiian picture-wing melanin; Huey 2000 documents the subobscura size cline.; reconstructed_in_script: λ_c = 1.92 µm is the slot assignment. Neighbour wavelengths 2.64 µm and 1.60 µm are γ retunings. | On a 96 µm arc the mode counts are 36 (silvestris), 50 (simulans), 60 (subobscura). | The plate annulus measures 67.57 µm (111 px scale bar = 100 µm), or 35.2 detail wavelengths per ring.; transfer_boundary: Silvestris and subobscura are catalog neighbours at 0 Ma, not phylogenetic ancestors. | The 1.92 µm law is not the 83 µm tergite-band model of slot 2701.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a published measurement of 1.92 µm granule spacing. | Does not claim the gallery plate is an electron micrograph of the clasper. | Does not claim GIF-to-plate CV similarity uniquely identifies D. simulans; the whole-fly control also scores 85.6.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2015.08.005>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1093/molbev/msaa232>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.287.5451.308>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0000487> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://codex.flywire.ai/>,
        <https://flybase.org/>,
